  "answer": "### Short Answer\nThe filing deadline for the individual annual income tax return in the Philippines is on or before April 15 of the following year after the taxable year.\n\n### Interpretation\n\n### Practical Meaning\nTaxpayers should ensure that their income tax returns are filed by April 15 to avoid penalties and interest for late filing. It is advisable to prepare and gather necessary documents well in advance of this deadline to facilitate timely submission.",
